{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play","id":1186864,"title":"HIgh Tier Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-16T16:20:29-08:00","id":1186864,"title":"HIgh Tier Play","content":"In the latest preview we are given rules for how Psions (Tier 2 Characters) can become Proxies (Tier 3 Characters). Extrapolating from these rules, if I as a SG, wanted to create my own little world, where Tier 4 Psychics are available, what should it require (Must have (x) at (y)), and what should it allow (May now raise (x) to (x+y), etc)? If you were in a game such as this, as a player, or as a SG, would you prefer Depth of power (More, PSI, Higher ratings of Aptitudes, etc), breadth (Higher ratings on Auxiliary Modes, etc), or some combination of the two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T18:25:47-08:00","id":1186891,"title":"","content":"Honestly without seeing what Proxie level powers can do I can't figure out what a Tier 4 Psion should look like.. Hell I'm not sure where a Tier 3 Nova becomes Tier 4 Aberrant, would that be Quantum 6? Is Max a Tier 3 character? Or would Time travel be the perview of a Tier 4 psion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T18:51:32-08:00","id":1186898,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how the developers are going to do it, but as I see it: Tier 1 - Normal Mortals, Tier 2 - Mesmer/Psion/Psiad (Psi1-5) Stalwarts (Quantum 1&amp;2), Talents (Mortal+), Tier 3 - Average Nova (Quantum 3-5), Proxy (Psi 6-7), Tier 4 - Godlike Nova/Prime Threat (Quantum 6+)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T19:26:45-08:00","id":1186906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1186898#post1186898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how the developers are going to do it, but as I see it: Tier 1 - Normal Mortals, Tier 2 - Mesmer/Psion/Psiad (Psi1-5) Stalwarts (Quantum 1&amp;2), Talents (Mortal+), Tier 3 - Average Nova (Quantum 3-5), Proxy (Psi 6-7), Tier 4 - Godlike Nova/Prime Threat (Quantum 6+)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly that's not really that helpful at getting a scale of what people can do. In 1e Quantum 6 powers cover &quot;can possess a machine&quot; at the low end with Quantum ten powers at the high end being &quot;Create universe&quot;<br /> <br /> Do we assume that Level seven is the top for psionic powers? That these are the same toys the Doyen would have? Or does their scale go to ten? IF so we have an easy break point for psion Tier 4 would be Psi 8 and filling in a few more powers.<br /> <br /> The other direction to go in is that the Doyen don't have psionic powers past 7 but rather have greater diversity in powers. They may freely mix and match whatever powers they want up to level 7.. <br /> <br /> So that leaves us with Psiads who.. we don't have mechanics for yet. Previously they were more versitile at the cost of specialization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T21:16:59-08:00","id":1186931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1186906#post1186906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly that's not really that helpful at getting a scale of what people can do. In 1e Quantum 6 powers cover &quot;can possess a machine&quot; at the low end with Quantum ten powers at the high end being &quot;Create universe&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>... No one is asking for you to design anything... What Tier 3 powers can do, and what Tier 4 powers might do, is do is irrelevant. I was asking for preferences as to a theoretical, nonexistent, home-brewed, 4th Tier Psychic... Would you prefer more power (Higher Modes), more diversity (Higher cap on Auxiliary Modes), some combination of the two, or something completely different, that is my question. And, given that we now know what the requirements are for Psions (Tier 2) to become Proxies (Tier 3), what requirements might there be to advance to this hypothetical, nonexistent, home-brewed, Tier 4... That's it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1186906#post1186906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we assume that Level seven is the top for psionic powers? That these are the same toys the Doyen would have? Or does their scale go to ten? IF so we have an easy break point for psion Tier 4 would be Psi 8 and filling in a few more powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of right now, yes, 7 is likely to be the max, but I don't care about that. Raising the cap on PSI to 8-10 is an obvious first choice, as to your second point, that's what I'm asking. Would you prefer higher level Modes, or better access to step outside of your Psionic Aptitude, unique powers, some combination of the aforementioned, or something else entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1186906#post1186906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other direction to go in is that the Doyen don't have psionic powers past 7 but rather have greater diversity in powers. They may freely mix and match whatever powers they want up to level 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I could care less about what aliens can do in general, and Doyen's in particular, what you are describing is one possibility for Tier 4, and quite possibly a good choice, as it's less work on my part, but is it the best option... we'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1186906#post1186906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that leaves us with Psiads who.. we don't have mechanics for yet. Previously they were more versatile at the cost of specialization.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't even know if it's possible for Psiads to go to Tier 3, let alone Tier 4, so I'm not as worried about them in this hypothetical scenario.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T22:10:01-08:00","id":1186938,"title":"","content":"I use Doyen as an example because they might count as &quot;Tier 4&quot; psychics. They clearly kept some tricks from the proxys. Since we know they &quot;locked' humanity into the apptitudes unnaturally with Prometheus chambers we can make some assumptions that ones that aren't tampered with might allow for Higher powered Psiads.<br /> <br /> In this case Tier 4 psychics would be Psi 8 and maybe run on the vague Psiad mechanics of Primary modes at 7, secondary Modes at 5? Or maybe all Modes at 7! How much does specialization matter? That's the problem without seeing psionic powers currently.<br /> <br /> Of course what if we want to keep the Psiad/Psion split all the way to the end? That would require more work hmmm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T20:19:49-08:00","id":1187201,"title":"","content":"Frankly with Novas or the Inspired you could just give them more points. Psions are designed to be more straightjacketed. The aliens wanted to limit humanity. Like the bit about wanting a horse strong enough to plow but to weak to kick. <br /> <br /> There aren't just powers. There's a limit on combining powers. A psion who was both a Clairsentient and a Psychokinetic might be level two but the Proxies might well fear them. <br /> <br /> You need more than power levels to define psions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-17-2018, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T20:53:25-08:00","id":1187204,"title":"","content":"My personal view is that there\u2019s nothing stopping higher Tiers existing under the Trinity Continuum concept. I have a few ideas towards that way, myself. However, it\u2019s way too early to begin building for higher Tiers when we haven\u2019t really finished rounding out what\u2019s possible at Tier 3 (novas), and have only scratched the surface for some antagonist builds at Tier 4 (Aberrants).<br /> <br /> In my own personal head space, humanity is destined for higher Tiers. However, Quantum powers tend to get their faster by their very nature (burn bright, burn quick), but this speed brings dangers and pitfalls along the way. Subquantum powers are the slower and safer way to reach these higher Tier levels, but when I say slower, I believe humanity was still several hundred to a thousand years off Psiads getting to Tier 3 (based on 1E Psiad builds, and assuming that level of power fits into Tier 2), let along humanity naturally growing into Tier 4+ via that route. THe Prometheus effect allowed us to skip quite a few speed bumps, but the trade off was that it\u2019s a form of Doyen control and psions (and Proxies) can and will never raise higher than Tier 3.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s entirely my own speculative thoughts on the matter, not endorsed or followed by OPP at all.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: I don\u2019t know how Talents fit into this head canon, or whether they can ever move to higher Tiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-17-2018, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T21:20:09-08:00","id":1187205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187204#post1187204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal view is that there\u2019s nothing stopping higher Tiers existing under the Trinity Continuum concept. I have a few ideas towards that way, myself. However, it\u2019s way too early to begin building for higher Tiers when we haven\u2019t really finished rounding out what\u2019s possible at Tier 3 (novas), and have only scratched the surface for some antagonist builds at Tier 4 (Aberrants).<br /> <br /> In my own personal head space, humanity is destined for higher Tiers. However, Quantum powers tend to get their faster by their very nature (burn bright, burn quick), but this speed brings dangers and pitfalls along the way. Subquantum powers are the slower and safer way to reach these higher Tier levels, but when I say slower, I believe humanity was still several hundred to a thousand years off Psiads getting to Tier 3 (based on 1E Psiad builds, and assuming that level of power fits into Tier 2), let along humanity naturally growing into Tier 4+ via that route. THe Prometheus effect allowed us to skip quite a few speed bumps, but the trade off was that it\u2019s a form of Doyen control and psions (and Proxies) can and will never raise higher than Tier 3.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s entirely my own speculative thoughts on the matter, not endorsed or followed by OPP at all.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: I don\u2019t know how Talents fit into this head canon, or whether they can ever move to higher Tiers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I recall reading <i>way</i> back when that the original fiction that was never completed was intended to tell the story of how the protagonist overcame the Doyen psion limits in that stubborn and indefinable way humanity somehow always manages to adapt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T20:44:45-08:00","id":1187448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187204#post1187204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit to add: I don\u2019t know how Talents fit into this head canon, or whether they can ever move to higher Tiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Higher Tier Paramorphs should exist.. and if that removes time powers from Novas well I'm ok with that.<br /> <br /> Max is clearly at least Tier 3 and I'm not a big fan of &quot;NPC ONLY&quot; scale..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T21:26:09-08:00","id":1187455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187448#post1187448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Higher Tier Paramorphs should exist</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? What purpose do they serve that isn't better covered by some other group? Talents are there to be the James Bond, or Jason Bourne. They're Human Plus... Lucky, Skilled, and Just that Good, but still on the edge of believable. Move them too far away from human, and you loose the whole point of having them there in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187448#post1187448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and if that removes time powers from Novas well I'm ok with that.</div> </div> </div> </div> =/= Does not equate. Just because X has Y, in no way means that Z can't have Y as well. TK, Telepathy, and pretty much all of the Psionic Aptitudes can be duplicated by Novas. Does that mean that they shouldn't have access to those powers? No, it's the way that they access them, and use them, that makes them unique experiences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187448#post1187448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Max is clearly at least Tier 3 and I'm not a big fan of &quot;NPC ONLY&quot; scale..</div> </div> </div> </div>While I nominally agree with you about &quot;NPC ONLY&quot; scale, I hate Mr Mercer with a passion, and I believe that Max is best left defined as someone who has seen visions of a possible future, and started the Aeon Society to help prevent it. No time travel, No Teleportation. I'd rather he never show up with stats then have rules for Tier 3 Paramorphs that gives everyone time travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T01:03:53-08:00","id":1187488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187455#post1187455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? What purpose do they serve that isn't better covered by some other group? Talents are there to be the James Bond, or Jason Bourne. They're Human Plus... Lucky, Skilled, and Just that Good, but still on the edge of believable. Move them too far away from human, and you loose the whole point of having them there in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>a Tier 2 Talent doesn't automatically upgrade to Tier 3. You can play perfectly good games at Tier 2 with them. Same with Psions, there might be a rare few who climb up to Proxy status but most are staying at Tier 2 forever. Stalwarts don't necissarily have to become Novas, you can keep them in Tier 2 forever. <br /> <br /> <br /> The separation of Psion/Nova powers is a pure in universe creation that has no basis outside it that exists purely to build plot of off. Tier 3 Talents are an interesting plot hook dangling out there. If you don't want to use them. Don't.3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> =/= Does not equate. Just because X has Y, in no way means that Z can't have Y as well. TK, Telepathy, and pretty much all of the Psionic Aptitudes can be duplicated by Novas. Does that mean that they shouldn't have access to those powers? No, it's the way that they access them, and use them, that makes them unique experiences. </div> </div> </div>We have no idea what Novas can and can't do in this edition. Its entirely possible there's &quot;Psion only&quot; or &quot;Psion do this better&quot; effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I nominally agree with you about &quot;NPC ONLY&quot; scale, I hate Mr Mercer with a passion, and I believe that Max is best left defined as someone who has seen visions of a possible future, and started the Aeon Society to help prevent it. No time travel, No Teleportation. I'd rather he never show up with stats then have rules for Tier 3 Paramorphs that gives everyone time travel. </div> </div> </div>I disagree. If you don't like them don't use them. Max is already in setting. I for one welcome our Time Lords, because if there's a Tier 3 Talent it is the Doctor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T02:42:47-08:00","id":1187501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187488#post1187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Tier 2 Talent doesn't automatically upgrade to Tier 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you know? In reality, you don't, no one does, and you are most likely wrong about people not &quot;automatically&quot; upgrading their Tier when they meet the prerequisites. I take this from both Scion's Visitations (Different game, I know, but bare with me), Talent Creation (See Moment of Inspiration) and the Aeon preview document under Creating Advanced Characters &quot;Characters who meet these three prerequisites <b>automatically</b> become Tier 3 proxy-level characters.&quot;. Once you meet the prerequisites, you ascend. Nothing in the game thus far can lead to any other conclusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187488#post1187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can play perfectly good games at Tier 2 with them. Same with Psions, there might be a rare few who climb up to Proxy status but most are staying at Tier 2 forever. Stalwarts don't necissarily have to become Novas, you can keep them in Tier 2 forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that is the game (Adventure!) or social contract at your individual table, sure, but the rules are there for a reason, and it's not to look pretty. Unless the SG has stated otherwise at the beginning, it's reasonable for a player to assume that if they get their character to a point where they are meeting the prerequisites, that they will ascend to Tier 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187488#post1187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The separation of Psion/Nova powers is a pure in universe creation that has no basis outside it that exists purely to build plot of off. Tier 3 Talents are an interesting plot hook dangling out there. If you don't want to use them. Don't.3</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a point? Everything in the whole game is a &quot;pure in universe creation that has no basis outside it that exists purely to build plot of off.&quot; This may come as strange to you, but I really enjoy Talents. They are my favorite type of character in Adventure!. Therefore, someone coming along and trying to add blatantly magical powers onto my &quot;Has no powers, is just that good&quot; option is shitting where I eat, and I don't appreciate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187488#post1187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have no idea what Novas can and can't do in this edition. Its entirely possible there's &quot;Psion only&quot; or &quot;Psion do this better&quot; effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice shifting of the goalposts. You are basically rewording what I just said. Is English your first language, because if not, I'm willing to cut you a bit more slack on your lack of reading comprehension. To be clear, you said that you would be fine with Talents getting Time Travel even if it meant that Novas lost it. I said that just because one group gets something, doesn't mean that another group can't get a similar effect. There may very well be effects that are unique. There will definitely be strengths, and weaknesses, to every template. In all likelihood there will be effects that appear at higher, or lower, Tier based on the template chosen, and I'm perfectly ok with that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187488#post1187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. If you don't like them don't use them. Max is already in setting. I for one welcome our Time Lords, because if there's a Tier 3 Talent it is the Doctor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, I won't, and thus far they haven't mentioned Max doing any time travel so I'm okay with his continued existence. And you do realize that if you really want to play Dr Who, you already can with just the Trinity Core alone. After all, even the Time Lords required a T.A.R.D.I.S. (AKA Wondrous Object) There is no need to take the &quot;no powers&quot; template and give it powers just because one poorly written NPC in 1st edition had super powers because he had to be *super more most special then any PC ever*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T03:11:42-08:00","id":1187505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187501#post1187501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a point? Everything in the whole game is a &quot;pure in universe creation that has no basis outside it that exists purely to build plot of off.&quot; This may come as strange to you, but I really enjoy Talents. They are my favorite type of character in Adventure!. Therefore, someone coming along and trying to add blatantly magical powers onto my &quot;Has no powers, is just that good&quot; option is shitting where I eat, and I don't appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Has no powers, is just that good&quot; is expliclty <i>not</i> what Talents are in Trinity Continuum. It was one of the explanations of them in Adventure, but this time around, they are explicitly magic. They're reality manipulators, pulling things in from other dimensions. Flux is a measurable, quantifiable thing. It''s magic. It's just more subtle than the other superhumans in the setting.<br /> <br /> And Max is quite possibly sticking around as previously written given the coy comment <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186608-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-02?p=1187171#post1187171\">here</a>. So long as Max exists, I think there's a need for Tier 3 paramorphs as an option (Even if it's the sort of thing that you're not going to realistically progress to from a standard Talent, due to massive experience costs, or awkward requirements) because otherwise we've got the old White Wolf staple &quot;Our NPCs are cooler than your PCs&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T03:49:44-08:00","id":1187509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187505#post1187505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Has no powers, is just that good&quot; is expliclty <i>not</i> what Talents are in Trinity Continuum. It was one of the explanations of them in Adventure, but this time around, they are explicitly magic. They're reality manipulators, pulling things in from other dimensions. Flux is a measurable, quantifiable thing. It''s magic. It's just more subtle than the other superhumans in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;determining the difference between a normal human and a Talent is not an easy task&quot; The Developer PC who never ages, and teleports thru time and space, is very easy to tell apart from a normal human.<br /> <br /> &quot;Most Talents think they are normal people, just like everyone else except for some extraordinary attribute.&quot; &quot;Just as some people are more talented than others at more <b>mundane skills</b> \u2014 a piano prodigy or a math whiz \u2014 a Talent is inherently better at the <b>subconscious</b> manipulation of probability called \u201cluck\u201d <b>which all humans do</b>.&quot; &quot;Maybe a person is so skilled in noticing details and remembering them that people consider her a genius, or someone is always able to find the right time and place to never be noticed, passing through the world nearly invisible. These people are <b>masters of a craft</b>, inspired to <b>exceptional skill</b> or <b>extraordinary luck</b> by something in their lives.&quot; Traveling thru time is not an extension of any attribute, or skill. Show me the time travel attribute, or skill. What is the mundane roll to time travel? Being more talented at time travel is bullshit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187505#post1187505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Max is quite possibly sticking around as previously written given the coy comment <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186608-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-02?p=1187171#post1187171\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know Max exists, what I have an issue with is him having time traveling powers and calling him a Tier 3 Talent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187505#post1187505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So long as Max exists, I think there's a need for Tier 3 paramorphs as an option (Even if it's the sort of thing that you're not going to realistically progress to from a standard Talent, due to massive experience costs, or awkward requirements) because otherwise we've got the old White Wolf staple &quot;Our NPCs are cooler than your PCs&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you even bother to read my last paragraph? Let me quote it for you &quot;There is no need to take the &quot;no powers&quot; template and give it powers just because one poorly written NPC in 1st edition had super powers because he had to be *super more most special then any PC ever*.&quot; If Max has the ability to travel thru time, then he's no Talent. Call him something else.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T03:58:44-08:00","id":1187510,"title":"","content":"Opinions ... they differ.<br /> Take it to PM if you want to continue attacking each other, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T10:06:28-08:00","id":1187588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187501#post1187501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you know? In reality, you don't, no one does, and you are most likely wrong about people not &quot;automatically&quot; upgrading their Tier when they meet the prerequisites. I take this from both Scion's Visitations (Different game, I know, but bare with me), Talent Creation (See Moment of Inspiration) and the Aeon preview document under Creating Advanced Characters &quot;Characters who meet these three prerequisites <b>automatically</b> become Tier 3 proxy-level characters.&quot;. Once you meet the prerequisites, you ascend. Nothing in the game thus far can lead to any other conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't meet the prerequisites, Onyx path doesn't have 90 game ninjas to break into your house and force you to. <br /> <br /> <br /> If you look at the cost of going from a starting Psion to Tier 3 it will take roughly 2 years assuming weekly play. That is assuming you go straight for it and don't buy up things outside that. I have plenty of games I've finished in 2 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that is the game (Adventure!) or social contract at your individual table, sure, but the rules are there for a reason, and it's not to look pretty. Unless the SG has stated otherwise at the beginning, it's reasonable for a player to assume that if they get their character to a point where they are meeting the prerequisites, that they will ascend to Tier 3. </div> </div> </div>No its not. Its not reasonable at all. I don't play D&amp;D with the assumption I'm going to max level. I don't play Vampire with the assumption I'm going to Eat my Way down to Antedeluvian. I Play the story at hand. I play a D&amp;D game which runs from 1st to 6th level and if we complete the story I don't expect another 14 level(in 5e, more on others) of explicit game play if we finish our plot in those levels.<br /> <br /> But lets circle this back, as you consider all Rules manditory, the rules currently have Aeon games with a Mix of Talents and Psions. So lets have a group of 3 players, 2 playing Talents 1 playing a Psion. Do you A. Let Psion player just level up to Proxy Tier and let the Talent Players become sidekicks at best. B. say &quot;you can't level up to proxy tier this is a tier 2 game&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because I for some reason read the Tier rating as an explicit level you set at SG. That I say something like &quot;I'm running a Tier 2 Aeon game&quot; that no the psion player shouldn't at all expect to become Proxy level. That that is how the rules are intended to be read. Just like if I'm running a pure Trinity Core book game and someone says &quot;I want to play a Psion&quot; I'll say &quot;No&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have a point? Everything in the whole game is a &quot;pure in universe creation that has no basis outside it that exists purely to build plot of off.&quot; This may come as strange to you, but I really enjoy Talents. They are my favorite type of character in Adventure!. Therefore, someone coming along and trying to add blatantly magical powers onto my &quot;Has no powers, is just that good&quot; option is shitting where I eat, and I don't appreciate it. </div> </div> </div>They haven't? Talents stay the same. There COULD BE a paramorph Upgrade at Tier 3. You are the one who apparently is forced to use all Rules that ever exist even if they have nothing to do with what you want or the story you are running. <br /> <br /> There's ALL Sorts of way Tier 3 Paramorphs could be locked off. Maybe you need to go through a &quot;second origin event&quot; like Max and if you don't meet that you don't get special powers. Or perhaps you have to be met by a fellow Time Traveler.. there's all sorts of &quot;you don't just LEVEL UP&quot; to tier 3 options.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Tier 3 Paramorphs exist they aren't even going to be in the Core book. They are going to be off in theirown little separate rules. Maybe they will have theirown gameline I don't see how that will at all effect you playing Talents in every other Gameline there is.. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nice shifting of the goalposts. You are basically rewording what I just said. Is English your first language, because if not, I'm willing to cut you a bit more slack on your lack of reading comprehension. To be clear, you said that you would be fine with Talents getting Time Travel even if it meant that Novas lost it. I said that just because one group gets something, doesn't mean that another group can't get a similar effect. There may very well be effects that are unique. There will definitely be strengths, and weaknesses, to every template. In all likelihood there will be effects that appear at higher, or lower, Tier based on the template chosen, and I'm perfectly ok with that too. </div> </div> </div>I am trying hard not to insult you, so please stop trying to insult me. Stop taking things as personal insults and making this super emotional. I feel 1e Novas were perhaps too broadly capable, and would prefer them losing some of their broad power to make the different types show their differences more readily. This includes Tier 3 Paramorphs but also Psions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously, I won't, and thus far they haven't mentioned Max doing any time travel so I'm okay with his continued existence. And you do realize that if you really want to play Dr Who, you already can with just the Trinity Core alone. After all, even the Time Lords required a T.A.R.D.I.S. (AKA Wondrous Object) There is no need to take the &quot;no powers&quot; template and give it powers just because one poorly written NPC in 1st edition had super powers because he had to be *super more most special then any PC ever*. </div> </div> </div>The No powers Template is called &quot;Baseline&quot;. Talents have powers its right there in teh core. But hey lets look at &quot;Wondrous Objects&quot; would Talents be &quot;ruined&quot; if their &quot;Tier 3&quot; jump is being given a bunch of &quot;Talent only Gadgets&quot; from the Time Corps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T16:42:59-08:00","id":1187684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't meet the prerequisites, Onyx path doesn't have 90 game ninjas to break into your house and force you to.</div> </div> </div> </div>You stated that you don't automatically go up once you meat the prerequisites, I proved you wrong, so your response is to tell me this? No kidding... My argument was never that any character had to ascend to a higher Tier if the player didn't want to. My argument is that if a player wants to, all they have to do is meet them, and they are good to go, assuming that there isn't a social contract at the table prior to game start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the cost of going from a starting Psion to Tier 3 it will take roughly 2 years assuming weekly play. That is assuming you go straight for it and don't buy up things outside that. I have plenty of games I've finished in 2 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basic starting players are 52xp away from hitting the prerequisites for Proxy (Tier 3) play. Just so we're on the same page, let me break down the math. Starting PSI @ 3, Mode A @ 3, Mode B @ 1. Proxy Tier requires PSI 6, Mode A @ 5, and Mode B @ 3, that is it. The Path prerequisites are for starting at Heroic and Proxy xp levels. Therefore it takes 12xp per purchase of PSI for rating 4 &amp; 5, 24xp for Rating 6. Total thus far = 48xp. Mode A from 3-5 is 12xp, Mode B from 1-3 is 12xp. Total thus far = 72xp. Player characters start with an additional 20xp. 72-20=52xp remaining til potential proxy prerequisites can be met. Now, assuming 4xp average per game, 1 for short term goal (You determine this goal, and therefore it is well within grasp most game sessions), 1 for everyone getting their short term (if everyone helps each other reach their goals, then this one is easy to achieve), 1xp for using 1/2 the black pool in a scene (Completely player controlled, there is no reason that this isn't achieved every game), and 1 for story milestone (the focus of the session), this calculation doesn't even include the more occasional higher xp rewards. Therefore: 52/4 = 13, that leaves us with an average of 13 game sessions until any character can potentially get the prerequisites to become Tier 3. Therefore, assuming that you play once a week (your assumption), you are looking at 3 months of play time. How many games have you played that lasted at least 3 months?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No its not. Its not reasonable at all. I don't play D&amp;D with the assumption I'm going to max level. I don't play Vampire with the assumption I'm going to Eat my Way down to Antedeluvian. I Play the story at hand. I play a D&amp;D game which runs from 1st to 6th level and if we complete the story I don't expect another 14 level(in 5e, more on others) of explicit game play if we finish our plot in those levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again you are argueing against something that I didn't say. Let me ask you this, do you expect Prestige Classes in 3.5 assuming the DM hasn't said anything otherwise? How about Multi classing? If you reach the XP threshold for level 5, do you expect to level up? No where did I say that all games must reach Tier 3. All I have stated is that it's there, and well within grasp of those who are interested in it (so long as there isn't a preexisting social contract regarding it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But lets circle this back, as you consider all Rules manditory</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong, I consider all rules in the core book in use, unless otherwise agreed to before hand. Hence the use of the term &quot;social contract&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the rules currently have Aeon games with a Mix of Talents and Psions. So lets have a group of 3 players, 2 playing Talents 1 playing a Psion. Do you A. Let Psion player just level up to Proxy Tier and let the Talent Players become sidekicks at best. B. say &quot;you can't level up to proxy tier this is a tier 2 game&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because I for some reason read the Tier rating as an explicit level you set at SG. That I say something like &quot;I'm running a Tier 2 Aeon game&quot; that no the psion player shouldn't at all expect to become Proxy level. That that is how the rules are intended to be read. Just like if I'm running a pure Trinity Core book game and someone says &quot;I want to play a Psion&quot; I'll say &quot;No&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations, you just used textbook examples of the social contracts that I mentioned in the paragraph you quoted, therefore proving my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They haven't? Talents stay the same. There COULD BE a paramorph Upgrade at Tier 3. You are the one who apparently is forced to use all Rules that ever exist even if they have nothing to do with what you want or the story you are running.<br /> <br /> There's ALL Sorts of way Tier 3 Paramorphs could be locked off. Maybe you need to go through a &quot;second origin event&quot; like Max and if you don't meet that you don't get special powers. Or perhaps you have to be met by a fellow Time Traveler.. there's all sorts of &quot;you don't just LEVEL UP&quot; to tier 3 options.<br /> <br /> If Tier 3 Paramorphs exist they aren't even going to be in the Core book. They are going to be off in their own little separate rules. Maybe they will have their own game line I don't see how that will at all effect you playing Talents in every other Game line there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid points. My complete list of reasons for disliking the idea of Tier 3 Talents is long, and not worth sharing, but you are correct in that not everything has to be used, especially if agreed to by your individual group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying hard not to insult you, so please stop trying to insult me. Stop taking things as personal insults and making this super emotional.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't an insult. You have shown a clear, and severe, lack of ability to read and understand what I have written. Multiple times in this thread alone you have argued against things I never said and points I never made, shifted your stance once refuted, and argued in favor of my basic assumptions while acting like what you just said is in some way a refutation. Therefore, I assumed that English might not be your native language, and therefore I was willing to take the time necessary to make what I was writing clearer to someone who might not be as familiar with my mother tongue. When I ask someone if &quot;X&quot; is there native language, it is not meant as an insult, but as a request to know if I need to be more basic, and detailed, in my explanations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel 1e Novas were perhaps too broadly capable, and would prefer them losing some of their broad power to make the different types show their differences more readily. This includes Tier 3 Paramorphs but also Psions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously we disagree on this point, but I can understand where you are coming from. I just don't think putting artificial limitations on Novas will solve any more problems then it creates, or even help anything in the long, or short term.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The No powers Template is called &quot;Baseline&quot;. Talents have powers its right there in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this right here is the lack of reading comprehension that I'm talking about. There is a difference between &quot;In Game&quot; and &quot;Out of Game&quot;. Talents &quot;In Game&quot; don't have &quot;Powers&quot;, they are just individuals that are &quot;that skilled, lucky, or good&quot;. They are the Indiana Jones, Laura Croft, the cast of Leverage, Oceans 11, the A Team, and the Italian Job. Now, &quot;Out of Game&quot; it is required that there be some way to allow, and keep track of all the cool &quot;I'm just that good&quot; things your character can do, and how often you can do them. Therefore &quot;Out of Game&quot; they have &quot;Powers&quot; so that you have a way of representing how awesome your character is. That they have &quot;Out of Game Powers&quot; is no reason for giving &quot;In Game Powers&quot; to the template based on being, in the books own words: &quot;<i>Just as some people are more talented than others at more <b>mundane skills</b> \u2014 a piano prodigy or a math whiz \u2014 a Talent is inherently better at the <b>subconscious</b> manipulation of probability called \u201cluck\u201d <b>which all humans do</b>.&quot; &quot;Maybe a person is so skilled in noticing details and remembering them that people consider her a genius, or someone is always able to find the right time and place to never be noticed, passing through the world nearly invisible. These people are <b>masters of a craft</b>, inspired to <b>exceptional skill</b> or <b>extraordinary luck</b> by something in their lives.</i>&quot;, and as I said before: &quot;Traveling thru time is not an extension of any attribute, or skill. Show me the time travel attribute, or skill. What is the mundane roll to time travel?&quot; or, are you trying to claim that certain &quot;Lucky&quot; people just happen to control their own personal travel thru time/space/alternate realities, without devices of any sort, and that such a thing would not be considered obviously supernatural?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186864-high-tier-play?p=1187588#post1187588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But hey lets look at &quot;Wondrous Objects&quot; would Talents be &quot;ruined&quot; if their &quot;Tier 3&quot; jump is being given a bunch of &quot;Talent only Gadgets&quot; from the Time Corps?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you are describing is called Powered Science, it's in the Core rule book under Super Science. Though in the Core, Talents lack access to it, but giving it to them hardly makes sense, or makes them them Tier 3.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe they will do something unexpected, and totally in line with what a Talent is, that can still allow them to be considered Tier 3. There are some shows, such as Forever, that have otherwise ordinary characters that have &quot;that one supernatural thing&quot; that they cannot control, and maybe they can find a way to make it far more interesting then at will, no devices, time travel. I for one certainly hope so, but I'm not going to hold my breath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":".  *Edited for Grammer, Spelling, and Punctuation 02-20-2018, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T00:36:15-08:00","id":1187769,"title":"","content":"Hey folks, you\u2019re both passionate about Trinity and what you love, and I love that. But it\u2019s turning into an argument rather than a discussion. You both have different likes and dislikes - there\u2019s room for both in the Continuum. High Tier Talents, low Tier paramorphs, whatever. We can do both. Take the rules we like, apply them to our dimensions within the Continuum and run with that.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s been some misunderstanding on both sides. Let\u2019s all take a deep breath, and drop this particular back-and-forth for a moment. Okay?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a new backer preview tomorrow (or is that later today? What\u2019s the time difference again?) Sadly, it sounds like it\u2019s not going to include the Psi Rules (I know, I\u2019m as bummed as you are, just for different reasons), but we\u2019ll have more to talk about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}